From: Jeremy Kerr <jk@codeconstruct.com.au>
Date: Mon, 9 Feb 2026 15:27:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: mctp: ensure our nlmsg responses are initialised
Git-commit: a6a9bc544b675d8b5180f2718ec985ad267b5cbf
Patch-mainline: v7.0-rc1
References: CVE-2026-45930 bsc#1266730

Syed Faraz Abrar (@farazsth98) from Zellic, and Pumpkin (@u1f383) from
DEVCORE Research Team working with Trend Micro Zero Day Initiative
report that a RTM_GETNEIGH will return uninitalised data in the pad
bytes of the ndmsg data.

Ensure we're initialising the netlink data to zero, in the link, addr
and neigh response messages.

Fixes: 831119f88781 ("mctp: Add neighbour netlink interface")
Fixes: 06d2f4c583a7 ("mctp: Add netlink route management")
Fixes: 583be982d934 ("mctp: Add device handling and netlink interface")
Signed-off-by: Jeremy Kerr <jk@codeconstruct.com.au>
Reviewed-by: Simon Horman <horms@kernel.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260209-dev-mctp-nlmsg-v1-1-f1e30c346a43@codeconstruct.com.au
Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>
---
 net/mctp/device.c |    1 +
 net/mctp/neigh.c  |    1 +
 net/mctp/route.c  |    1 +
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/net/mctp/device.c
+++ b/net/mctp/device.c
@@ -70,6 +70,7 @@ static int mctp_fill_addrinfo(struct sk_
 		return -EMSGSIZE;
 
 	hdr = nlmsg_data(nlh);
+	memset(hdr, 0, sizeof(*hdr));
 	hdr->ifa_family = AF_MCTP;
 	hdr->ifa_prefixlen = 0;
 	hdr->ifa_flags = 0;
--- a/net/mctp/neigh.c
+++ b/net/mctp/neigh.c
@@ -218,6 +218,7 @@ static int mctp_fill_neigh(struct sk_buf
 		return -EMSGSIZE;
 
 	hdr = nlmsg_data(nlh);
+	memset(hdr, 0, sizeof(*hdr));
 	hdr->ndm_family = AF_MCTP;
 	hdr->ndm_ifindex = dev->ifindex;
 	hdr->ndm_state = 0; // TODO other state bits?
--- a/net/mctp/route.c
+++ b/net/mctp/route.c
@@ -1395,6 +1395,7 @@ static int mctp_fill_rtinfo(struct sk_bu
 		return -EMSGSIZE;
 
 	hdr = nlmsg_data(nlh);
+	memset(hdr, 0, sizeof(*hdr));
 	hdr->rtm_family = AF_MCTP;
 
 	/* we use the _len fields as a number of EIDs, rather than
